**Amendment (Observation representation measurement)** · `amend:devperf:compact-observation-measurement` The completed warm gate after (`amend:observe:compact-content`) has a 393,126-byte main log, compared with the reviewed 245,438,225-byte log; complete observation streams and addressed payloads are retained separately, so this is log routing and encoding rather than content suppression. The same five instrumented documents steps, fixed-point-write, datasets, documents, determinism-datasets and determinism-documents, total 9.660407 seconds, compared with the reviewed 3.80 seconds. The observed wall is slower; no speedup or causal regression attribution is claimed from differently loaded single gates. Structured decoding, content addressing and artifact delivery now do work that the earlier representation did not. Both functional gates passed, and these walls never change a result. The untracked work report records the final gate separately rather than replacing this original sample.
